{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Mountains</b> — And the word is from the root of אנכי הרה שבהם, in which are metals, as: ומהרריה תחצוב נחשת; iron is taken from earth, and hills without metals. And afterward he mentioned the plants, and began with עץ פרי and כל ארזים, which do not yield fruit, and afterward he mentioned —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 148, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Job 28:2 (הרה שבהם) and Deuteronomy 8:9 (ומהרריה תחצוב נחשת); both rendered in Hebrew as quoted. The comment trails off with an em dash, as the Hebrew ends with 'ואחר כן הזכיר —' incomplete."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:07.648128549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}